{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/826334-xp-requirements","id":826334,"title":"XP Requirements?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-08T15:32:52-08:00","id":826334,"title":"XP Requirements?","content":"Sooo.... I was running a Scion campaign, with games every other week, for about 6 months or so. We eventually dropped it when we realized the EXP required to get from Hero to God would require us to play the existing campaign for around an additional 5-7 years non-stop. That is a long time in terms of a single campaign, IMO... Was I doing something wrong and will this be an issue in the new version?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Yes, yes, yes... I know it is a horror game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11143-feonorx","name":"Feonorx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T20:09:52-08:00","id":826497,"title":"","content":"When we ran our home game we addressed that by creating mission-based rewards, but ultimately it just depends on how quickly you want your game to progress. Like in typical WW systems, the exp table as written tends to be kinda slow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T06:41:55-08:00","id":826785,"title":"","content":"One of the things that I think is common is that Legend is assigned by the ST instead of paid for. That freed up a lot of xp for our group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T08:40:15-08:00","id":826848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Feonorx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/826334-xp-requirements#post826334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was I doing something wrong and will this be an issue in the new version?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how it was in 1e, yes.<br /> <br /> 2e is moving to a different system. It's got a linear experience system currently, but I'm also investigating a milestone-type experience system to reflect shifting competence.<br /> <br /> Either way, Legend won't be paid for with XP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T13:52:08-08:00","id":827066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/826334-xp-requirements?p=826848#post826848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's how it was in 1e, yes.<br /> <br /> 2e is moving to a different system. It's got a linear experience system currently, but I'm also investigating a milestone-type experience system to reflect shifting competence.<br /> <br /> Either way, Legend won't be paid for with XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was one of the best changes in EX3 for something so small, tying Essence increases to set intervals, and having mote pools be strictly determined by what essence you are at, no other factors. A much more elegant way of doing things, and so simple you gotta wonder why nobody thought of it in the first place.<br /> <br /> Doing something similar in Scion 2e is a really good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T06:01:50-08:00","id":827456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/826334-xp-requirements?p=826785#post826785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things that I think is common is that Legend is assigned by the ST instead of paid for. That freed up a lot of xp for our group.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That sounds like the best option, actually. When you have the option to buy Legend, I can't help but imagine somebody going <b>&quot;I demand to be more Legendary!&quot;</b> and suddenly he's got people flocking to praise and worship him. It's amusing, but doesn't make much sense from a logical perspective.<br /> <br /> Depending upon the length of your chronicle and how many chapters your story has, it may be appropriate to give the players a point of permanent Legend after each completed session, assuming they did something worthy of the advancement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-10-2016, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T06:12:33-08:00","id":827464,"title":"","content":"An additional thing to look at is to bump up the End-of-Session reward for DemiGod and God (5/10/15). This will allow people to look at higher level Boons more seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T23:05:53-08:00","id":830053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/826334-xp-requirements?p=826848#post826848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's how it was in 1e, yes.<br /> <br /> 2e is moving to a different system. It's got a linear experience system currently, but I'm also investigating a milestone-type experience system to reflect shifting competence.<br /> <br /> Either way, Legend won't be paid for with XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. On the flip side, one of the nice things from 1e was that one could start at Demi-God or even God level. It certainly seemed as if that version put on on the specific path to Godhood while making the XP cost to get there almost prohibitive. From a design perspective, I'm curious to see how this plays out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Yes, yes, yes... I know it is a horror game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11143-feonorx","name":"Feonorx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}